# What never belongs in the image build context. The context is the repository root, because the
# Downloads gRPC client compiles sidecar/torrent/proto/torrent.proto — everything else is trimmed here
# so the daemon is not handed build output, dependencies, history or anything that could carry a secret.

# ---- build output and restored dependencies (the image restores its own) ----
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
web/dist/
artifacts/
TestResults/
*.trx
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml

# ---- history and tooling state ----
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github/
.vs/
.idea/
.claude/
.codegraph/
.config/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# ---- not compiled into the application image ----
tests/
poc/
**/*.md

# ---- secrets and local state: never in a build context, not even to be ignored later ----
# Every pattern is `**/`-prefixed on purpose: a bare `.env` is anchored at the context root, so it would
# leave web/.env.local — whose VITE_* values `vite build` inlines into the served bundle — in the context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
# The development settings hold a development database credential and a developer's own paths. The publish
# step excludes them as well; both matter, because either one alone is a single edit away from shipping.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.*.Local.json
**/secrets.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.key

# ---- runtime data and scratch ----
data/
media/
generated/
scratch/
tmp/
*.log
*.fastresume

# ---- packaging files the build itself does not read ----
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
